  "title": "03.30",
  "content": "[[File:0330.png|right]] \n03.30\n\n==The Corn Fields==\n\nRegion: The Corn Fields.\n\nConnects to: 03.29, 04.30, 04.31, 15.11, 29.14 and 33.00.\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\">\n</p>\n\n==Overview==\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">This area is covered in ripe fields of corn which seem to grow all year round. The farmers of this crop dwell in a small and dusty village at the cent</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt; font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">er</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> of the hex. Insular in the extreme, they are also dangerously hostile to anyone who they think they can defeat. However, a show of force will easily cow them into submission. </span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">The corn farmers drug and kidnap unlucky adventurers who pass through their town. They then steal all their victims' po</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">s</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">sessions and, bizarr</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">e</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black; mso-themecolor:text1\">ly, pull out all their teeth, before dumping them in the nearby Thorny Gulch</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family: \"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> (04.30)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black; mso-themecolor:text1\">. The teeth are ground up</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> against the surface of their rocky god (03.29)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt; font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> and used to fertilize the corn crops; each</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> stalk of</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black; mso-themecolor:text1\"> corn ha</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt; font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">ving</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> a different property depending on the type of tooth</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> used</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">. Molar-corn, for example, grants the ability to crush objects between one's palms. Corn from wisdom teeth is used by shamans of the corn people, though its exact properties are still a secret. </span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">It is a strange fact of the corn farmers that they consider teeth to be a rich treasure, but have no use for gold or magic items. These objects make them a target for bandits who are rife in the area, so they dispose of them by dropping them down </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">a certain</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> old well </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">(</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black; mso-themecolor:text1\">04.31</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt; font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">. There, the treasure is consumed by the sentient black sphere known as the Nothing.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">One would assume that such treasure is irretrievably lost. However</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\"> some years ago </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">Dormond of the Crooked Oak </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">(04.31) </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">returned to the Shuttered City bearing a single gemstone of unique color but relatively low value. He claimed that he had traced this gem's lineage from the Hoard </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">b</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black; mso-themecolor:text1\">ank </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt; font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">(33.00) </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\";mso-fareast-font-family: \"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black; mso-themecolor:text1\">to a party of adventurers lost in the southwest over a century ago. This was proof, he claimed, that matter could be retrieved from within the </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">s</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">phere. Before he could explain more, however, he disappeared.</span></p>\n\n==Connection==\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">-Grimvlech the Smiler lost his original teeth here (15.11).</span></p>\n\n==Hooks==\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">-What other types of corn can be grown, and who would pay for them?\n</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">-Tell me more about the bandits of the southwest.\n</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">-There must be an incredible treasure hoard hidden inside that Sphere! But how to get it out?\n</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6pt;\">\n</p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-fareast-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\"; color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">-What's in Thorny Gulch? Will adventurers survived being dumped there naked and unarmed?\n</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">\n</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-bottom:.5gd\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"CenturyGothic\",\"sans-serif\"; mso-bidi-font-family:\"TimesNewRoman\";color:black;mso-themecolor:text1\">\n</span></p>\n[[Category:Hex]]\n[[Category:The Cornfields]]",
